line	<str>Speak to the Chemist. He will give you the touch paper.</str>
line	
line	<str>You will find Chancy, Da Vinci and Hops around a fire outside the Chemist's house.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give Chancy the Liquid honey.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give Da Vinci the Ethenea.</str>
line	
line	<str>Give Hops the Sulphuric broline.</str>
line	
line	<str>Teleport or travel to Varrock.</str>
line	
line	<str>Travel to the fenced area to the south-east of the bank (south-eastern Varrock). The guard will search you, but you will be able to pass freely with the plague sample and touch paper in your inventory.</str>
line	
line	<str>(Optional) Speak to Asyff, the Fancy dress shop owner, in the building south-east, to get a free priest gown (top and bottom) and equip it. Alternatively, purchase a priest gown (top and bottom) from him and equip it.</str>
line	
line	<str>Go to the Dancing Donkey Inn.</str>
line	
line	<str>Talk to Hops, Da Vinci and Chancy to get the vials back. Make sure you have the free inventory space.</str>
line	
line	<str>With your Priest gown equipped head to Guidor's house in the south-east of the fenced area.</str>
line	
line	<str>Speak to Guidor, tell him Elena has sent a sample that needs to be processed.</str>
line	
line	<str>Return to Ardougne and speak to Elena.</str>
line	
line	<col=000080>Go to the uk=1 of <col=800000>Ardougne Castle</col> and speak to <col=800000>King Lathas</col>.</col>
done	<str>To begin speak to Elena in East Ardougne (directly west of shortcut log).</str>
done	
done	<str>Speak to Jerico in the house just south of the northern Ardougne bank (The house with pigeon cages in the backyard).</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the cupboard to obtain bird feed (click continue or the bird feed won't be added to your inventory).</str>
done	
done	<str>Grab a pigeon cage from the backyard (note: if you are planning on doing One Small Favour, grab an extra 5 pigeon cages).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go south-west of Ardougne Castle and speak to Omart.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go north to the small watchtower along the wall, in front of the gates to West Ardougne.</str>
done	
done	<str>Stand in the corner where the two spiked fences meet.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use bird feed on the watchtower fence.</str>
done	
done	<str>Click open on the pigeon cage in your inventory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip your gas mask.</str>
done	
done	<str>Run south from the watchtower and speak to Omart. After a slight delay, you will arrive in West Ardougne.</str>
done	
done	<str>Head around the headquarters to the north-eastern area with the vat and mangle.</str>
done	
done	<str>Squeeze through the fence into the backyard.</str>
done	
done	<str>Pick up the rotten apple.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the rotten apple on the cauldron.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go back through the fence.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to Nurse Sarah's house, south-west of the West Ardougne church.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search cupboard in northern part of the house for a medical gown.</str>
done	
done	<str>Equip the medical gown, go back to the headquarters and open the door.</str>
done	
done	<str>Go upstairs and kill a mourner. A key will automatically be placed in your inventory.</str>
done	
done	<str>Use the key on the gate to get into the caged room.</str>
done	
done	<str>Search the crate third from the left on the northern wall to find Elena's distillator.</str>
done	
done	<str>With 3 empty inventory spaces, return to Elena and give her the distillator (via Ardougne Teleport, Skills necklace teleport to the Fishing Guild, over the wall by Kilron, or via the sewers from the Plague City quest).</str>
done	
done	<str>Go to the Chemist in south-western Rimmington (you can take a ship from Captain Barnaby at the Ardougne Dock directly to Rimmington for 30gp or use a teleport as the vials won't break upon teleportation anymore)</str>
